# tg_mhd (CUDA FP32)  hydro_noslip_nofield_n512_re2000_va1.41421  N=512 Re=2000 h=6.14793083e-03 delta=2.23606798e-02 delta/h=3.637107 layers=256 written=31
# THE ENERGY BUDGET against wall distance. Per probe, one row per term: t, the term,
# its contribution to the BOX MEAN from each of the layers 0..30 (layer k: the nodes
# k cells from the nearest wall, the slab [(k-1/2)h, (k+1/2)h]) and from the rest of
# the box beyond them, so a row sums to the box average. Paper units: energies in
# v0^2, rates in k0 v0^3. With eK = |u|^2/2 and eM = |B|^2/2,
#   d eK/dt = lor + advK + pres + difK - visc
#   d eM/dt = S + advM + difM + cmpM - ohm
# lor = u.(j x B); S = B_i B_j d_j u_i; advK, advM = -u.grad eK, -u.grad eM;
# pres = -u.grad p, p = cs^2 rho/u0^2; difK = nu div(u x w); difM = eta div(B x j);
# cmpM = -|B|^2 div u + (u.B) div B; visc = nu |w|^2; ohm = eta |j|^2. The scheme is
# weakly compressible, so a layer's terms close only to a residual.
# row 'vol': each column's share of the volume
# vol 5.859360e-03 1.164997e-02 1.155859e-02 1.146758e-02 1.137693e-02 1.128664e-02 1.119670e-02 1.110713e-02 1.101792e-02 1.092906e-02 1.084057e-02 1.075244e-02 1.066466e-02 1.057725e-02 1.049019e-02 1.040350e-02 1.031716e-02 1.023119e-02 1.014557e-02 1.006031e-02 9.975416e-03 9.890879e-03 9.806702e-03 9.722884e-03 9.639427e-03 9.556329e-03 9.473590e-03 9.391212e-03 9.309193e-03 9.227534e-03 9.146235e-03 6.829279e-01
